.TH NEWFS_EXT2FS 8
.SH NAME
newfs_ext2fs \- create a supported ext2 filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B newfs_ext2fs
[\-b 1024|2048|4096] [\-L label] [\-m percent] special [blocks]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes /sbin/mke2fs directly with revision 1, 128-byte inodes, and features
filetype and sparse_super only. Default block size is 1024 bytes; reserved
space defaults to 5 percent. Labels are at most 16 bytes. Percent is an integer
between 0 and 50. An optional positive blocks count is measured in the selected
block size. Regular-file images are supported. Mounted targets and failed
mount-table/device inspection are refused before execution.
The selected partition capacity is inspected read-only before the formatter
starts; unavailable or invalid queries and oversized explicit counts are
refused. No legacy whole-drive size fallback is used. Internal -F permits
raw character devices and regular-file images after these checks. Existing
regular images may grow with an explicit count within checked native offset/block-address bounds. Device counts always remain within their selected partition.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the formatter status; invalid options return 16 and inspection or
child-process failures return 8.
.SH SEE ALSO
fsck_ext2fs(8), mount_ext2fs(8), mke2fs(8)
